# Central pinned refs for in-lab Paintbot player builds.
#
# One source of truth so builds are reproducible. Sourced by tools/build_player.sh.

# The shared player SDK that stencil (Python) builds against — installed from the
# coworld-tools monorepo's GitHub source tarball (the `players/` subdirectory). Kept
# in sync with the root pyproject.toml [tool.uv.sources] tarball SHA so local `uv run`
# and the built image run the SAME SDK (SpriteV1 bridge included). To bump: set the SHA
# here + in pyproject.toml and `uv lock`. A literal `main` is a Docker cache trap (the
# pip layer caches on the URL string), so build_player.sh resolves `main` via ls-remote.
PLAYERS_SDK_REF=e8921a6b18484030d8704277e4c52d3aae5c8917

# The coworld-ctf game commit stencil's sim-rule constants were derived from
# (config.py: speeds, aim, gun timing, spray geometry, item respawns). Paintbot and
# CTF share this repo/binary; the paintbot LEAGUE redeploys often (deployed paintbot
# 0.7.178 at lab creation, 2026-08-03 — repo main 1633b7e). Unlike beacon there is
# NO map bake to invalidate: all map facts arrive on the wire per episode. Bump when
# verifying constants against a newer deployed game version.
PAINTBOT_GAME_REF=1633b7e
